  "title": "Proofing House",
  "rules": [
    "Carry one tray at a time. Pick an accessible tray within one cell; put it on the free cell ahead. Shelf pickup requires an open cupboard door.",
    "Knead a loose raw batch on a nearby board. Seeded batches and existing board trace leave seed trace on both the batch and the surface.",
    "Wash an unoccupied dirty board to clear its trace, or discard and wash a carried batch at the sink. Each uses one of eight shared wash-water units.",
    "A closed, unvented cupboard targets warmth three; ventilation targets two, and an open door targets one. Warmth changes by one per tick.",
    "Closed-shelf proof grows by warmth minus one per tick. Other proofing batches rise only on every third tick. Proof above twelve spoils a batch.",
    "The oven holds one tray. Baking freezes proof; three hot ticks make a loaf ready, and seven hot ticks burn a loaf left in the oven.",
    "Plain service accepts proof five through eight and no seed trace. Seeded service accepts proof seven through ten. Serve at the hatch.",
    "Shared loaf rewards plus owner/server bonuses compete with individual action and disposal costs. All rules use the native state and actions."
  ],
